# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables for blind-nav.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# RULES:
#  - Secrets (API keys) are SERVER-ONLY. They must NEVER be prefixed with
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_ and must never be read from client/browser code.
#    They are consumed only inside server route handlers / server modules.
#  - Only variables that are genuinely safe to ship to the browser may use
#    the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#  - `.env.local` is git-ignored. Never commit real keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- AI vision provider (server-only) --------------------------------------
# Google Gemini API key, used only by the server-side vision provider.
# Obtain from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Default Gemini model id used by the server-side provider.
# (Confirm the current model id against official docs before use.)
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Optional alternate provider (server-only), wired behind the same abstraction.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Dev-only: force the canned fixture vision provider even when a key is set, so
# the pipeline can be exercised without calling Gemini. "1" or "true" to enable.
# Ignored in production. Fixtures are also used automatically in development
# when no GEMINI_API_KEY is configured.
# VISION_FIXTURES=1

# --- Application (safe for client only if truly non-sensitive) --------------
# Example of a public, non-secret value. Leave unset unless needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development